id: pm-pivf
title: Resolve validate duplicate issue-code GH-209 warning without changelog drag
description: "pm validate metadata warns validate_metadata_duplicate_issue_codes for GH-209 shared by closed items pm-1byt (exit-13 top-level-await fix) and pm-25se (OTLP export follow-up). Both live in shipped release buckets; renaming either title now would move it into [Unreleased] because pm-changelog buckets by updated_at (known trap). Resolve by either (a) teaching issue-code dedupe to exempt explicit 'follow-up' titled items so distinct logical work sharing a GH code is not flagged, or (b) performing the rename in a dedicated tracker-only migration where the changelog is regenerated and reviewed in the same commit."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: metadata,tracker-governance,validate
created_at: "2026-07-04T19:01:47.101Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T20:37:43.701Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "pm validate reports duplicate_issue_codes_count: 0 (or the GH-209 pair is exempted by an agreed follow-up rule with a spec); changelog:pm:check stays green in the same change; no closed item silently migrates release buckets.; The by-design exemption reads the typed derivation channel, not only the scalar parent: within a code group an item carrying a discovered_from, supersedes, or incident_from row that points at another item in the same group is dropped from collision detection, resolved against the same-code group only, exactly as the existing parent rule is; A negative control proves the rule is not over-broad: a same-code pair with no edge is still reported, and a same-code pair joined only by a related row is still reported, because related asserts similarity and not lineage; One upstream issue may map to more than one item when the report surfaced more than one defect, expressed as a typed relation between the items rather than tolerated by naming, and the duplicate-code check passes on that structure"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: low
confidence: high
